            <div xml:id="d336">

                <pb facs="0580" n="476" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg476"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.8810/1159: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at Berlin
                        (Messersmith)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-10-21T13:00:00-05:00">October 21, 1933—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Roosevelt Steamship Company alleges that pressure is being and has been
                    brought to bear upon German importers and exporters to confine <pb facs="0581"
                        n="477" xml:id="pg477"/> their shipments to German ships. It is not known
                    whether this pressure, which it is claimed has reached a stage of intimidation,
                    comes from official or party sources. I wish you would discreetly investigate
                    this matter and, if you are able to obtain the necessary concrete information,
                    take it up directly and informally with the appropriate authorities.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
